  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Title: Oracle
  Description: 'Mentioned in many a myth and play, the Oracle of Delphi was a conduit
    to Apollo, the god of Light and Truth. The Oracle herself, known as the Pythia,
    consulted with the gods by inhaling vapors of the Castalian Spring on which her
    temple was built. This would send the Pythia into a frenzy, and from this ecstatic
    state, the Pythia would produce her visions. The Oracle''s predictions were highly
    regarded among many Mediterranean societies until 393 AD, when the Roman Emperor
    Theodosius I ordered the temple''s closure. '
